      "agentRuntime": "langgraph",
      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's how **long rests** work in Frosthaven:\n\n---\n\n## Long Rests\n\n**When to declare:** During the **Card Selection** step, instead of selecting two ability cards, a character may declare a long rest — but only if they have **at least two cards** in their discard pile.\n\n**Initiative:** A long rest is performed on initiative **99** and constitutes the character's **entire turn** for the round.\n\n**When performing a long rest, follow these steps in order:**\n\n1. **Lose one card of your choice** from your discard pile and return the remaining cards to your hand. *(mandatory)*\n2. **Perform *Heal 2*, self.** *(optional)*\n3. **Recover all spent items.** Items can even be used during the same turn they are recovered. *(optional)*\n\n---\n\nThe key advantages of a long rest over a short rest are that you **choose** which card to lose (rather than losing one at random), you get a heal, and you recover all your spent items. The trade-off is that you give up your entire turn for the round and act last at initiative 99.\n\n*(Rulebook, passage 125)*",
