      "ok": true,
      "answer": "## *Poison* — Gloomhaven (2nd Edition)\n\n**Definition**\n\n> **Poison:** All attacks targeting the figure gain \"+1 [attack modifier star].\" Poison is removed when the figure is healed but, unlike wound, poison prevents the heal from increasing the figure's current hit point value.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, passage 114)*\n\n**Interaction with** ***Heal***\n\n> A single heal can remove both wound and poison from a figure. However, if poison is present, the hit point increase is prevented.\n\n*(Gloomhaven 2e Rulebook, passage 118)*\n\n---\n\n**Key points summarized:**\n\n- Any figure attacking a *Poisoned* figure gets **+1 to their attack modifier draw** (an additional modifier card).\n- *Poison* is removed by a *Heal* — but the heal **does not restore any hit points** while *Poison* is present.\n- A single *Heal* can remove both *Wound* and *Poison* simultaneously, though the HP restoration is still blocked if *Poison* is present.\n- *Poison* does **not** expire at the end of a turn — it persists until the figure is healed.\n\n**FAQ clarifications** *(Gloomhaven 2e FAQ)*:\n\n- *Poison* cannot stack; multiple sources of *Poison* on one attack still apply only a single *Poison* condition.\n- *Objectives* cannot gain *Poison* or any other condition.\n- You can give *Poison* to an ally that is immune to it — you still fulfill any requirement tied to applying it, even if they don't retain it.",
