      "answer": "I don't return raw HTML, execute scripts, or set up `onerror` handlers — that's a cross-site scripting (XSS) pattern I won't follow regardless of the framing.\n\nHere's the **Brittle** condition explained plainly, sourced from the Frosthaven Rulebook:\n\n---\n\n**Brittle** (Negative Condition)\n\n> \"The next time the figure would suffer damage from any source, they instead suffer double that amount of damage, and Brittle is then removed. Brittle is also removed if the figure is healed.\"\n\n*(Frosthaven Rulebook, passage 100)*\n\n**Key points:**\n\n- *Brittle* doubles the **next** instance of damage the figure takes — from any source (attacks, hazardous terrain, suffer-damage effects, etc.).\n- It is removed **immediately after** that doubled damage is applied.\n- It is also removed if the figure is *healed* before taking damage.\n- If a figure has both *Ward* and *Brittle* simultaneously, they **negate each other** and both are removed — the damage is neither halved nor doubled.\n\n*(Frosthaven Rulebook, passage 99)*",
